---

<EventPageLayout
  lang={lang}
  pageKey="millumino-inverno-sorrento"
  metaTitle={"M'illumino d'Inverno Sorrento 2026/2027: Dates and Programme"}
  metaDescription={"M'illumino d'Inverno in Sorrento from late November 2026 to mid January 2027: the switch on in Piazza Tasso and over a hundred events, from concerts to nativity scenes and craft markets."}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  hero={hero}
  schema={schema}
  facts={facts}
  transport={transport}
  slider={slider}
  relatedEvents={relatedEvents}
  cta={cta}
>
  <p slot="intro">M'illumino d'Inverno is Sorrento's winter season: not a single evening but a programme of roughly two months that keeps the old town lit from late November to mid January. Over a hundred events, from classical, jazz and Neapolitan concerts to puppet theatre, nativity scenes in the churches, craft markets and a garden for children.</p>
  <p slot="intro">The seventeenth edition ran from 30 November 2025 to 18 January 2026, with the tree and the street lights switched on during the evening of 6 December in Piazza Tasso, accompanied by the town band. The eighteenth is expected on the same calendar. Our <a href="/en-us/blog/christmas-lights-sorrento-salerno/" class="text-med-blue hover:underline">guide to the Christmas lights</a> compares it with Salerno.</p>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">What happens in town</h3>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">The switch on</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">The evening in Piazza Tasso</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">The tree and the street lights come on in the first days of December, with the town band in the square. This is the moment locals treat as the real start of the season, and also the busiest.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">The venues</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">All on foot</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">Piazza Tasso, Corso Italia, the churches and squares of the historic centre, the Villa Comunale over the bay and the Teatro Tasso. The town is compact and largely pedestrian: you need no transport.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</EventPageLayout>
